  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Above average temperatures today as a warm front \nbrings scattered light showers through early to mid afternoon, \nbefore a cold front generates a round of more substantial rain \nshowers later tonight through the first half of Friday.\n\nNose of 30-40 knot LLJ impinging on deeper moisture is producing \nscattered light showers across western NY to start the morning ahead \nof a warm front nearing the area. Warm front will progress northeast \nthrough western NY this morning, before moving through the North \nCountry this afternoon. Expect main area of light showers to finish \ncrossing western NY this morning, then move through the North \nCountry from mid morning through early to mid afternoon, with mainly \ndry weather areawide by later this afternoon as the main axis of \nmoisture shifts north of the region. Strong WAA pattern/cloud cover \nwill limit mixing potential of the stronger winds off the deck, \nhowever at least partial mixing along with a tightening pressure \ngradient ahead of an approaching cold front will elevate \nsouthwesterly flow. This will be especially true northeast of the \nLakes, where winds could gust up to 30 mph, especially across the \nNiagara Frontier.\n\nA sharper trough will then dig across the upper Great Lakes forcing \nthe aforementioned cold front southeast through western and \nnorthcentral NY later tonight into Friday morning. While PWAT values \nwill be nearing the 100th percentile for this time of year, along \nwith a stout 35-45 knot LLJ, showers will be mainly anafrontal and \nthus not be able to take full advantage of the more plentiful \nmoisture and much stronger forcing ahead of the front. Thus, while \nthere will be a period of beneficial showers, the heavy \nrainfall/flooding threat will be near zero. The main window for more \npersistent showers will be late tonight through midday/early \nafternoon Friday just behind the cold front, with a general one-\nthird to two-thirds of an inch of rainfall expected across western \nand northcentral NY. A few widely scattered light showers may linger \nin the wake of the cold front Friday afternoon, otherwise dry and \nseasonable weather is on tap for the upcoming weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Below normal temperatures with frost potential early \nnext week.\n\nA strong cold front with cross the area Sunday night, ushering in \nthe coolest airmass we've seen since last spring. 850mb temperatures \nwill plunge to near 0C or even a below during the first part of next \nweek, with daytime highs not getting out of the 50s for much of the \nregion, and possibly only upper 40s for highs across the Tug Hill \nand western Dacks by Tuesday.\n \nStrong upper level trough axis will cross the area Monday, possibly \nproducing a few showers, otherwise mainly dry weather is expected. \nThe main impact will be frost potential Monday night, and possibly \nagain Tuesday night.",
